#====================================================================
# DRAFT-levmar-2.6-official-source-incomplete-tls-chain
# — 官方源服务端 TLS 证书链不完整（缺中间 CA）时，curl/conan/python 一律
#   CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED；判别法 = openssl s_client -showcerts 数证书 +
#   Verify return code 21 + 同 CA 对正常主机成功；处置 = 换用作者官方页列出的
#   官方入口（sha256 必须逐字一致），官方入口为明文 http 时属 PF7「官方托管
#   例外」须 PR 说明；辅助 = 按内容 sha256 预置共享下载缓存（不随 PR 进 CI）
# 触发事件: levmar 2.6 适配（conan source 阶段首错 unable to get local issuer
#           certificate；官方源 www.ics.forth.gr）
# 路径: Path B（知识库扩展）
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-levmar-2.6-official-source-incomplete-tls-chain
trigger_tool:           conan|curl|openssl|python
phase:                  download
error_signature:        unable to get local issuer certificate|certificate verify failed|
                         unable to verify the first certificate|Verify return code 21|
                         SSLError\(SSLCertVerificationError|ConanException. Error downloading file

severity:               2
category:               network, conan, download, tls, ohos
match_keywords:         unable to get local issuer certificate, CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED, incomplete certificate chain, missing intermediate CA, openssl s_client verify code 21, conan source download failure, official source unreachable, non-github official host, mirror map miss, official download page alternate entry, same-sha256 official http direct link, official hosting exception PF7, core.sources:download_cache, download cache preseed, sha256 keyed cache, Sources correctly downloaded

title:                  An official source whose TLS chain omits the intermediate CA fails every verified client (curl/conan/python) with "unable to get local issuer certificate"; prove it is server-side by counting the certificates sent by openssl s_client and by fetching a known-good host with the same CA bundle, then fall back to the alternate official entry listed on the author's own download page (sha256 must match byte-for-byte; a plain-http official entry is a declared PF7 official-hosting exception), never by disabling verification

root_cause:             The upstream host (www.ics.forth.gr, the levmar 2.6 official tarball site) sends only TWO certificates in the TLS handshake: the leaf CN=ics.forth.gr plus HARICA TLS RSA Root CA 2021, while omitting the intermediate "GEANT TLS RSA 1" that actually signed the leaf. Standard clients (curl, python ssl, conan's downloader) therefore abort with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED / "unable to get local issuer certificate"; openssl s_client reports "Verify return code: 21 (unable to verify the first certificate)". The trap is that this signature is usually caused by a client-side problem (no ca-certificates on OHOS, missing CA bundle), so the reflexive fix (-k / --no-check-certificate, install a CA package) is wrong here and hides a server-side misconfiguration that will hit every clean CI worker too. Two discriminators separate the two root causes: (1) openssl s_client -showcerts | grep -c "BEGIN CERTIFICATE" shows 2 while a healthy chain shows leaf + intermediates; (2) the SAME CA bundle verifies other hosts (curl.se 200, api.gitcode.com/conan.cnb.cool complete TLS), so the bundle is not the problem.

affected_scope:         Any package whose conandata.yml points at an official/authoritative https host that serves an incomplete certificate chain, i.e. any non-GitHub official host. Aggravating factor found on levmar 2.6: the CI-side mirror rewrite in ci/conan/build_and_test.sh only maps a fixed host list (github.com, *.gnu.org, *.gnome.org, cdn.kernel.org, sourceforge, pythonhosted, curl.se, ftp.jaist.ac.jp, ...), so such a host gets NO mirror fallback and the CI pre-download step (plain `curl -sL --retry 3`, no -k) fails as well, leaving conan's own download to fail too. Verified: levmar 2.6 (https://www.ics.forth.gr/~lourakis/levmar/levmar-2.6.tgz, sha256 3bf4ef1e...bad7, 81143 bytes).

solution: |
  Step 1 — prove it is server-side before touching the recipe (this decides
  whether the fix belongs in the recipe at all):

  ```bash
  # a) how many certificates does the server send, and what does openssl say?
  openssl s_client -connect <host>:443 -servername <host> -showcerts </dev/null 2>/dev/null \
    | grep -c "BEGIN CERTIFICATE"
  openssl s_client -connect <host>:443 -servername <host> </dev/null 2>/dev/null \
    | grep "Verify return code"
  #   2 certificates + "Verify return code: 21" == missing intermediate CA

  # b) rule out the local CA store: the SAME bundle must verify a known-good host
  curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://curl.se/ca/cacert.pem     # 200 = bundle OK
  ```

  Step 2 — look for another OFFICIAL entry of the SAME upstream site, starting
  from the author's own download page (this is the fix that survives CI):

  ```bash
  # the author's download page itself is often served from a host whose chain
  # works, and it links the tarball relatively
  curl -sS http://<author-host>/<pkg>/ | grep -o '<a href="[^"]*\.tgz">'
  # candidate entry: must be plain 200 (no redirect to the broken https host)
  curl -sS -o cand.tgz -w "code=%{http_code} size=%{size_download} redirect=%{redirect_url}\n" <candidate>
  # THE gate: content must be byte-identical to the sha256 already in conandata.yml
  python3 -c "import hashlib,sys;print(hashlib.sha256(open('cand.tgz','rb').read()).hexdigest())"
  ```

  Keep the `sha256` field UNCHANGED (integrity pinned by content hash, independent
  of the transport). The entry must belong to the upstream/author site itself —
  never a third-party proxy/mirror/pool/repack. Measured example (levmar 2.6):
  `https://www.ics.forth.gr/...` fails, the author page
  `http://users.ics.forth.gr/~lourakis/levmar/` ("Latest: levmar-2.6.tgz") gives
  `http://users.ics.forth.gr/~lourakis/levmar/levmar-2.6.tgz` -> 200 / 81143 bytes
  / same sha256 3bf4ef1e...bad7.

  Step 3 — if that official entry is plain http, preflight PF7 flags it
  (`PF7 源URL闸(R39): ... 明文 http 源（R39 要求 https）`). PF7's own wording is
  "确属官方托管例外须 PR 说明并 --no-preflight 跳过": declare the exception in
  the PR body (symptom, proof of officialness, the two identical sha256 readings,
  two repro commands) and skip explicitly. Never skip silently, never `-k`.

  Step 4 — verify with a REAL fetch: move the download-cache entry aside first so
  the build cannot be satisfied from cache, then require this line in the build log:

  ```
  Sources correctly downloaded from <new URL>
  ```

  (conan raises ConanException on a sha256 mismatch, so that line also proves the
  content check passed.)

  Secondary/local-only mitigation (经验库 §12.55): preseed the sha256-keyed shared
  download cache (key = CONTENT sha256 `s/<sha256>`, no `.dirty` marker, valid
  sidecar JSON whose `references` cover the requested URL and the recipe refs,
  proof = `retrieved from local download cache`). It only greens the machine that
  holds the cache: the cache does NOT ship with a PR, so CI stays red — that is
  exactly how levmar 2.6's first CI run failed, and on that链路 the CI pre-download
  fallback is additionally dead because the worker has no `curl` at all
  (`[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'curl'`).

fallback: >
  If (and only if) the local CA store legitimately lacks a well-known ROOT that
  the server does send, install/extend the CA bundle (see E034/E185). For an
  incomplete SERVER chain no client-side trust change is legitimate in this
  repository: `curl -k` / `--no-check-certificate` / `verify=False` and any
  NON-official http address are forbidden (PF7 blocks plain http/file:// and a
  14-domain mirror blacklist; disabling verification also defeats the sha256
  provenance of the tarball). Acceptable paths, in order: (1) another entry of the
  SAME official/author site whose content hashes to the same sha256 — for a
  plain-http official entry use the declared PF7 official-hosting exception
  (PR explanation + explicit skip); (2) a same-sha256 authoritative mirror URL as
  a second item in the conandata url list; (3) otherwise stop and report the
  external blockage. Never change the sha256 to accommodate another artifact.

verify_builds: "#PR-pending（levmar 2.6，本 PR）"
verification_cmd: >
  (1) openssl s_client -connect www.ics.forth.gr:443 -servername www.ics.forth.gr -showcerts </dev/null | grep -c "BEGIN CERTIFICATE"  -> 2
  (2) curl -sSL -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" https://www.ics.forth.gr/~lourakis/levmar/levmar-2.6.tgz  -> code=000 / curl: (60) SSL certificate problem: unable to get local issuer certificate
  (3) curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "code=%{http_code} redirect=%{redirect_url}" http://www.ics.forth.gr/~lourakis/levmar/levmar-2.6.tgz  -> code=301 redirect=https://www.ics.forth.gr/... (dead end)
  (4) curl -sS -o cand.tgz -w "code=%{http_code} size=%{size_download}" http://users.ics.forth.gr/~lourakis/levmar/levmar-2.6.tgz  -> code=200 size=81143
  (5) python3 -c "import hashlib;print(hashlib.sha256(open('cand.tgz','rb').read()).hexdigest())"  -> 3bf4ef1ea4475ded5315e8d8fc992a725f2e7940a74ca3b0f9029d9e6e94bad7 == conandata sha256
  (6) conan create (download-cache entry moved aside) -> "Sources correctly downloaded from http://users.ics.forth.gr/~lourakis/levmar/levmar-2.6.tgz" + verdict PASS + test_package TEST PASSED

limitations: >
  1) The alternate official entry only exists if the upstream site actually
     publishes one; always start from the author's own download page and prove
     byte-identity via sha256, otherwise the "fix" silently swaps the artifact.
  2) A plain-http official entry means the transport is not authenticated; the
     pinned sha256 is what preserves provenance. Declaring the PF7 official-hosting
     exception is mandatory, and the exception must be revisited once upstream
     repairs its chain (switch back to https and drop the exception).
  3) The sha256-keyed cache preseed only helps the machine that holds the cache
     (经验库 §12.55); CI workers do not share it, so it can never be the CI fix.
  4) The signature is shared with genuinely client-side CA problems; always run
     the discriminators first, otherwise the wrong owner (recipe) gets the blame.
  5) Reaching the alternate host on port 80 from the CI worker is not provable
     from a build machine; if CI is still red, read the first real error before
     attributing it.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           prove-server-side-then-use-alternate-official-entry-with-identical-sha256
rec_description:        先用 openssl s_client 证书计数/Verify 21 + 同一 CA 对正常主机成功，判定为服务端证书链不完整；再从作者官方下载页找**同一官方站点**的其他入口，取到文件后 sha256 必须与 conandata 记录值逐字一致才可改用（sha256 字段不动，完整性由内容哈希固定）；该入口若为明文 http 则按 PF7「官方托管例外」在 PR 正文说明并显式跳过；把下载缓存预置降为仅本机辅助手段；禁止 -k / 非官方 http / 改 sha256
rec_command:            openssl s_client -connect <host>:443 -servername <host> -showcerts </dev/null 2>/dev/null | grep -c "BEGIN CERTIFICATE"; curl -sS -o cand.tgz -w "code=%{http_code} size=%{size_download} redirect=%{redirect_url}\n" <candidate official entry>; python3 -c "import hashlib;print(hashlib.sha256(open('cand.tgz','rb').read()).hexdigest())"; grep -F "Sources correctly downloaded from" <build log>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual (conandata.yml url -> alternate official entry, sha256 unchanged; PF7 official-hosting exception declared in PR) 

